1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,730
Why is ambulance written backwards?

2
00:00:03,270 --> 00:00:04,030
It's not a mistake.

3
00:00:04,370 --> 00:00:06,330
It's written for one person: the driver

4
00:00:06,330 --> 00:00:08,000
stuck right in front of it.

5
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,120
When a siren screams behind you, you don't

6
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:11,760
turn around. You glance up...

7
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,040
at your mirror.

8
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:15,040
And a mirror flips everything left to

9
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:17,360
right. A normal word would look backwards.

10
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:19,580
So the word is printed flipped.

11
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:21,620
The official US ambulance spec even

12
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:22,590
requires it.

13
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:23,840
Backwards on the van...

14
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:26,080
but in your mirror, it reads AMBULANCE.

15
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:27,540
Did you ever notice?
